							<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><img src="/pics/2112/blueflame.gif" /><strong>Welcome to the Guild Bank</strong>&nbsp;</font></p> <p align="center"><font size="5">ANNOUNCEMENTS/UPDATES:</font></p> <p align="left"><font size="4">12/18/04 Lots of research has gone into valuing the items that have been donated so far. I truly appreciate every donation!! However, there is now the massive task of figuring out how to distribute/warehouse it all - fairly, of course! I am working with the War Council on how to do this, but meanwhile I am adding a page of items we have as well as what I've found to be the prices found in bazaar and on common merchants. I will link each of the items so that clicking on it will take you to Allakhazam's listing of what it is and how it is used. Thanx for your patience; I'm old and slow and this is a pretty big undertaking that I want to get done right. Once all is in place, it will be simple to maintain (hopefully).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Spud</font></p> <p><font size="4"><strong><em></em></strong></font>&nbsp;</p> <p><font size="4"><strong><em>Celticspud</em></strong> is currently serving as the guild banker, but is no longer&nbsp;using his character Celticdruid for that purpose. Instead, he has created a new character called<strong> <font color="#ffff00">Dtbanker</font></strong>.</font></p> <p><font size="4">All items and money are located on that character, and arrangements can be made online with Celticspud&nbsp;to take donations when they are online or through the Guild Bank forum.</font></p> <p><u><font size="4">To obtain an item or borrow from the guild bank;</font></u></p> <p><font size="4"><u>PLEASE NOTE THAT WE ARE OUTFITTING MAIN CHARACTERS ONLY - for now.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;We want to make sure that the items are available to the Main Characters 1st. Once we ensure that everyone's Main Character is taken care of, then somewhere down the line we can afford to look at outfitting alts.</font></p> <p><font size="4"><u><strong>Getting an item</strong></u> - must be a needed item for a particular purpose such as creating a spell, enhancing an item, etc. After 30 days in the bank, these items can be purchased for the going rate in the bazaar that day.</font></p> <p><font size="4"><strong><u>Spells</u></strong> - To get a spell from the bank, it must be a spell that your <em><strong><font color="#ee82ee">Main Character</font></strong></em> needs, and you must have achieved that level to get it. For example, a member who has a level 45 Druid main, and&nbsp;a 35 Cleric alt would be able to get level 45 Druid spells from bank, but not level 46 or greater until that character reaches the level of the spell. Also, the Cleric alt would not qualify to draw spells from the Guild Bank as alts are supposed to be "mentored" by your Main Character. This sounds restrictive, but as we progressively get stuff in the bank, there's going to be a lot of demand for little supply. Thanx for understanding.</font></p> <p><font size="4"><u><strong>To borrow money from the bank</strong></u>, there must be approval by at least<strong> 4</strong> officers <em><strong>confirmed with each other</strong></em>, and there will be no interest charged. However, repayment MUST be made within 1 week as there are many of us in the guild and needs are great though amounts are limited.</font></p> <p><font size="4">We are currently reviewing how Raid Points will be used. Watch for update. 2 ideas are a.) can turn in points for plat, and b.) can use RP's for loot. Nothing is firm and your suggestions on the Forum Pages will be greatly appreciated!</font></p> <p><font size="4">Currently, the bank has (as of <font color="#9acd32">12/12/04</font>):</font></p> <p><font size="4">PLAT = <font color="#ffff00"><strong>36,929 plat</strong></font></font></p> <p><font size="4">ITEMS: (This section will move soon to a seperate page on site)</font></p> <p><font size="4"> <table style="WIDTH: 369pt; BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="492" border="0" x=""> <colgroup> <col style="WIDTH: 118pt; mso-width-source: userset; mso-width-alt: 5741" width="157"> <col style="WIDTH: 80pt; mso-width-source: userset; mso-width-alt: 3913" width="107"> <col style="WIDTH: 171pt; mso-width-source: userset; mso-width-alt: 8338" width="228"> <tbody> <tr style="HEIGHT: 12.75pt" height="17"> <td class="xl24" style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; WIDTH: 118pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; HEIGHT: 12.75pt; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent" width="157" height="17"><strong><u><font face="Arial" color="#f5f5dc" size="2">SPELLS:</font></u></strong></td> <td class="xl24" style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; WIDTH: 80pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent" width="107"><strong><u><font face="Arial" color="#f5f5dc" size="2">WORDS:</font></u></strong></td> <td class="xl24" style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; WIDTH: 171pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent" width="228"><strong><u><font face="Arial" color="#f5f5dc" size="2">ITEMS:</font></u></strong></td></tr> <tr style="HEIGHT: 12.75pt" height="17"> <td style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; HEIGHT: 12.75pt; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent" height="17"><font face="Arial" color="#ffff00" size="2">Blast of Poison</font></td> <td style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"><font face="Arial" color="#ffff00" size="2">Coersion</font></td> <td style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8; BORDER-LEFT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-BOTTOM: #d4d0c8; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"><font face="Arial" color="#ffff00" size="2">Mask of Malediction</font></td></tr> <tr style="HEIGHT: 12.75pt" height="17"> <td style="BORDER-RIGHT: #d4d0c8; BORDER-TOP: #d4d0c8